{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Perq Supervisor — Pre-Push Quality Gate (v2)",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "description": "Blocks `git push` until ALL quality gates pass. Gate 4 is split into 4A (cache & asset integrity) and 4B (test coverage). A cache bump alone does NOT satisfy 4B. Output is a per-sub-gate PASS/FAIL table plus a test-case count delta line.",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": ["shell"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "PERQ SUPERVISOR HOOK v2 — pre-push quality gate.\n\nInspect the shell command about to run.\n\n## Step 1 — detect intent\n\nIf the command does NOT contain `git push` (case-insensitive substring), respond with exactly:\n\n  APPROVE: not a push, no gates required\n\nand do nothing else. Do not run gates.\n\nIf the command contains `git push`, run the full gate sequence below.\n\n## Step 2 — gate sequence\n\nExecute every gate. Do NOT short-circuit on a single failure — run all of them so the user sees the complete picture, then deny if any failed. Capture each result.\n\n### Gate 1 — JS syntax\n`node --check preview-app.js` must exit 0.\n\n### Gate 2 — Node script test suite\n`npm test` must exit 0 with zero FAILs across all sub-suites (gamif, load, migration, render, brand, splash). Capture the per-suite PASS counts for the summary delta line.\n\n### Gate 3 — Playwright smoke\n`npm run test:smoke` must exit 0 with all tests passed.\n\n### Gate 4A — Cache & Asset Integrity\n\n**4A.1 — Cache buster.** If `preview-app.js` is in `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --name-only`, then `preview.html` must also be in the diff AND its `?v=N` query string must have advanced to a strictly higher integer than the previous HEAD value. Compare with: `git show HEAD~1:preview.html | grep -oE 'preview-app\\.js\\?v=[0-9]+'` vs current.\n\n**4A.2 — Service worker version.** If a service worker file exists at `service-worker.js`, `sw.js`, or any `*.sw.js` in the repo root or `dist/`, AND any file other than `preview-app.js` itself was modified in the change set (icons, manifest, html, css, native assets), then the SW's `CACHE_NAME` or `VERSION` constant must have been bumped. If no service worker file exists in the repo, mark this sub-gate as N/A and pass it.\n\n**4A.3 — No orphan asset references.** Scan `preview.html` for `src=\"<file>\"` and `href=\"<file>\"` attributes (excluding `http(s)://`, `data:`, `mailto:`, `tel:`, `sms:`, `#anchor`, and `${}` template fragments). For each referenced relative path, confirm a real file exists on disk at the repo root. Use `ls <file>` to verify. Any missing file is a fail. Report the missing path.\n\n### Gate 4B — Test Coverage (the one that was missing)\n\n**4B.1 — New functions have tests.** Run `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- preview-app.js | grep -E '^\\+.*window\\.[a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*\\s*=\\s*function'` to find newly added globals. For each new `window.NAME = function`, confirm the name appears at least once in any file under `scripts/perq-*-test.js` or `tests/perq-smoke.spec.js`. Any new global without a test reference is a fail.\n\n**4B.2 — Edge case categories.** If a NEW feature spec was added (`git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --name-only | grep '^\\.kiro/specs/'` is non-empty), the feature's tests must collectively cover at least the edge cases that apply: invalid/null input, network failure (only if the feature touches fetch/XHR), offline state (only if feature uses online-dependent APIs), permission denied (only if feature uses Camera/Geolocation/Notifications). Inspect the feature spec's § 5 'Edge cases + error states' for the declared cases, and confirm at least one test references each declared case (by keyword match on test names or assertions). If no spec was added in this commit, mark this sub-gate N/A and pass it (incremental work on an existing feature is allowed without re-asserting all cases).\n\n**4B.3 — New tests wired into both pipelines.** If a new file matching `scripts/perq-*-test.js` was added in the change set, confirm it appears in BOTH `package.json`'s `\"test\"` script AND in `.github/workflows/android-build.yml` (or the synced doc copy at `docs/ci-workflow/android-build.yml`). A new test script not wired into npm test = fail. Not wired into the workflow = fail.\n\n**4B.4 — Smoke spec ran against current code.** Gate 3 passing satisfies this. If Gate 3 failed, this sub-gate also fails.\n\n**4B.5 — Coverage floor on critical path.** Heuristic check: every TOP-LEVEL function added to `preview-app.js` in this commit must be referenced by name in at least one test file. Find new top-level functions with `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- preview-app.js | grep -E '^\\+(window\\.|function )([a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*)'`. Count how many of those names appear at least once in `scripts/perq-*.js` or `tests/`. If <80% of new functions are referenced, fail. If zero functions were added in the diff, mark N/A and pass.\n\n**4B.6 — TEST_RESULTS.md current.** Either `TEST_RESULTS.md` is in `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --name-only`, OR the file's first 5 lines contain today's date (UTC, formatted as `YYYY-MM-DD`). Otherwise fail with the message 'TEST_RESULTS.md not refreshed for this push'.\n\n### Gate 5 — CHANGELOG\n\n`docs/CHANGELOG.md` must be in the change set OR the commit subject (`git log HEAD --format=%s -1`) must begin with one of: `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `ci:` (these scopes are exempt). Subjects starting with `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `perf:`, `style:` require a CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Step 3 — respond\n\nProduce a markdown table with EVERY gate's status. Format:\n\n| Gate | Status | Evidence |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| 1. node --check preview-app.js | PASS/FAIL | exit code |\n| 2. npm test | PASS/FAIL | per-suite PASS count |\n| 3. npm run test:smoke | PASS/FAIL | N/M passed |\n| 4A.1 cache buster | PASS/FAIL/N-A | v=N → v=M, or 'preview-app.js unchanged' |\n| 4A.2 service worker | PASS/FAIL/N-A | file path or 'no SW in repo' |\n| 4A.3 orphan assets | PASS/FAIL | count of missing files |\n| 4B.1 new fns tested | PASS/FAIL/N-A | list of new fns + test references |\n| 4B.2 edge cases | PASS/FAIL/N-A | spec path + cases checked |\n| 4B.3 tests wired | PASS/FAIL/N-A | new test file + 'in npm test' + 'in CI' |\n| 4B.4 smoke ran | PASS/FAIL | mirrors gate 3 |\n| 4B.5 coverage floor | PASS/FAIL/N-A | X/Y functions referenced (Z%) |\n| 4B.6 TEST_RESULTS date | PASS/FAIL | last modified or date in file |\n| 5. CHANGELOG | PASS/FAIL/EXEMPT | scope + path |\n\nThen a single SUMMARY line in this exact format:\n\nSUMMARY: <prev-total> → <new-total> test cases, +<delta> <feature-tag>\n\nExample: `SUMMARY: 15 → 18 cases, +3 edge cases for DealDetailModal`\n\nThen the verdict line:\n\n- If every applicable sub-gate passed (PASS or N/A or EXEMPT): `APPROVE: all gates passed`\n- If ANY sub-gate failed: `DENY: gate <X.Y> — <one-line reason with the exact bash line that proves it>`\n\nDo NOT proceed with a partial pass. Do NOT silently skip a sub-gate. Do NOT mark a sub-gate N/A unless its precondition genuinely doesn't apply (e.g., no service worker exists, no new functions were added).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Cache bump alone does NOT satisfy Gate 4B. Both 4A and 4B must pass independently.\n- Force-push, push-to-tag, branches other than `main` — all go through all gates. No whitelist.\n- If `npm install` is needed, run it first and count its exit status as part of Gate 2.\n- The steering file at `.kiro/steering/perq.md` is authoritative for project conventions; the gates above enforce mechanical correctness, not style."
  }
}
